n: two profiles in one file.** `authored_node` (write boundary — `confidence` *forbidden*, `status` pinned to `candidate`) and `stored_node` (at-rest, `confidence` required). This is what makes \"confidence is DERIVED, never authored\" structural rather than policy — a writer literally cannot express it. Root `$ref`s `stored_node`, not a `oneOf`, because a `oneOf` root would accept the authored-confidence fixture and destroy the invariant.\n\n**Interfaces** — all 17 §4.2 fields with keywords and clause derivation, 9 canonical regexes, the conditional rules (`canonical ⇒ evidence ≥ 1`; `refuted ⇒ non-null falsifier`), a transcribable schema skeleton, and the manifest contract.\n\n**State machines** — node epistemic status (with the frequency-promotion edge shown as *absent* and no state exiting to deletion), the confidence lifecycle, and the fixture verdict flow.\n\n**Fixture corpus** — 14 valid / 19 invalid (gate needs 12 / 8; margin is deliberate). Coverage closes over all 12 node types, 4 statuses, 4 author kinds, 3 evidence kinds, both profiles, both nullable fields in both states. Each invalid fixture is exactly one mutation of a named valid sibling.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n- **`format` is annotation-only in draft 2020-12.** A schema relying on `format: date-time` alone would silently accept `\"2026-08-08 12:00:00\"`. The design carries an explicit RFC-3339 pattern as the assertion, pins UTC `Z` (two spellings of one instant would break `corpus_hash` reproducibility per §5.1 r3), and adds test T7 as a canary.\n- **The manifest with `expect_error_path` is not ceremony.** Without asserting *why* an invalid fixture failed, a fixture that fails incidentally is a false pass — the corpus reports green while testing nothing.\n\n## Not done, deliberately\n\nI wrote nothing outside `design/`. The schema, fixtures, and test module are `sakg/`- and `tests/`-tree writes owned by BUILDER @ IMPLEMENT, and the four `accept` commands are VERIFY-stage evidence — running them now would fail and would misrepresent build evidence as design output. §11 is the transcription checklist; §10 records the four commands verbatim.\n\nEvidence emitted: `design_coherent` — assumptions A1–A10 plus open questions OQ-1–OQ-3 surfaced (PAEOS-6), all seven L09 perspectives covered, and a conservation audit mapping every field and every invariant to a fixture and a test, with four gaps (GAP-1–GAP-4) declared against named downstream owners rather than left silent.","ttft_ms":1810,"ttft_stream_ms":905,"time_to_request_ms":102,"type":"result","duration_ms":527058,"uuid":"f4d2b858-0eaf-4ee1-8dd0-b917c2426c89"}
